  "details": "1. Open VRChat.\n\n2. Go to an instance with people. (I've tried 20ish people on Luminescent Ledge and 40ish people on Foundry EUFuria)\n\n3. Enjoy yourself for some time.\n\n4. Observe that the game have crashed\n\nSometimes I crash before get loaded into the world, sometimes I can stay for 10s of minutes. Usually a couple of seconds.\n\nThings I tried:\n\n- sfc /scannow\n\n- Verify integrity of SteamVR and VRC\n\n- SteamLink and VirtualDesktop. Even Desktop mode crashes!\n\nSometimes there's a crash dump, complaining about UnityPlayer.dll trying to write to a forbidden area\n\nIf helpful, I can upload the logs and dump files\n\nNot that long ago I was able to attend a Foundry club event with 80 people, with the only filter being liimted to seeing the nearest 21 people. \n\nNow with more limitations (disabled shaders, etc) still unplayable most of the time.\n\nRAM and VRAM usage seemed fine, roughly below 70% so I don't think I could've ran out of them.\n\nPC:\n\nAMD Ryzen 5800X3D\n\n32GB RAM\n\nAMD 6950XT, up to date driver\n\nWindows 11",
